  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF TWO NMB FOCAL SPECIES SO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will improve the conservation status of Red Knot and Hudsonian Godwit in southern Patagonia in Argentina. The objectives are to: 1) build and consolidate local support for conservation actions; 2) expand the area and the degree of protection of urban natural reserves; and 3) increase community awareness through innovative methodologies, such as social marketing and reducing barriers to positive behavior change. The project will reduce the most significant threats to key shorebird areas, including dumping of waste and the disturbance of birds by vehicles, pets and recreational activities.</narrative>
  </description>
